  "_read_this_before_comparing": "These are L1 scores and they are only comparable to each other. The nine clips measured on Sep 5 were finished renders and scored 46-56 with a clean dark/bright split. These four are 720p budget renders of dark-ground compositions and they all land at 46-49 — the tier flattened the luminance advantage rather than the compositions losing it. Do not read a 47 here as the same thing as a 47 there.",
  "_what_L1_did_show": "Every one of the four peaks in its last three seconds and every one is weakest in the hook window: hooks 30-33 against overalls 46-49. The shot order buries its best second at the end, which is right for a film and wrong for a post. S11 is the exception that proves the rule — it peaks at second 7 and carries the lowest mind-wandering of the four (0.604), because it is the one shot that gets darker and closer as it runs. Sustain is 98-100 across the board, so retention still needs no work."
 },
